<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center" class="tborder" style="border-bottom: 0;">
	<tr class="titlebg">
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="15%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/topic/hot_post.gif" alt="" />
			Author
		</td>
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="85%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			Topic: Quellious: A Brief History &nbsp;(Read 773 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1087" title="View the profile of Ravenark">Ravenark</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 3<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1087"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:admin@quellious-collective.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1496.msg15876#msg15876"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1496.msg15876#msg15876">Quellious: A Brief History</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> March 29, 2005, 09:54:35 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I thought about putting this in the other thread but decided to start a fresh one.<br /><br />As many of you are aware, Rodcet is soon to be merged into Quellious. I know right off this is quite a blow to many of you. Long ago, I was also a member of the Rodcet Nife server (I&#039;m going to say one phrase and leave it at that &quot;MoOooOoOoOoOoOoOoooooo!!!&quot;). While it pains me to see the Rodcet Nife server name poof, I&#039;m happy to see that they will be united with Quellious.<br /><br />By far, the most unique an endearing part of Quellious is our community. It&#039;s what keeps the server together and what brings many people back from retirement after retirement for more.<br /><br />In 1999, when Quellious was fresh out of it&#039;s bubble wrapped server box, Quellious Quarters was founded. For a time it served to be a great community for the people of the server. Sadly, over time, some of the site administrators assumed this to mean they should have some sort of control or &quot;power&quot; over the in game world of Quellious. This idea was soon rejected and in a fit the administrators of the time nuked the forums and the community. Out of the ashes formed Quellious Collective. It was formed by a group of people who wanted nothing more than a community. No special treatment or recognition. Myself, Raalf, and Havusin have been the admins since that beginning.<br /><br />We learned a lesson from the mistakes of the previous admins. The community belonged to the actual members and no one else. That single driving principle is what has kept us running strong since 2000.<br /><br />Not too long ago, we recognized a growing issue. We had a huge community, people who loved to hang out and post what they feel and what they think. They were drawn together because of EverQuest but stayed because of each other. However, new games were on the horizon. The close community would be split all over many new games. It was then we decided (with the agreement of the community) to keep everyone together. It was then that we launched some serious production into a new website and forums. <br /><br />The goal is to keep those from Quellious who went to play WoW, EQ2 or EQ1, together. We picked our servers together (with only some mild *cough massive* confusion). For EQ2 we picked Permafrost, for WoW we picked Doomhammer and Icecrown (heh long story). As people split to branch out into the new games, they stayed together. Probably our proudest moment ever. The ability to keep everyone together despite where they go.<br /><br />The site is nearing it&#039;s full completion. With the help of our very talented artist admin Sceleris (we really only made him an admin because he&#039;s good with crayons, don&#039;t tell please), we&#039;ve put together quite a display. The only obstacle has been getting 3d imagery and rendering to work on a website at any resolution (You&#039;ll notice we&#039;ve all become accomplished alcoholics and I&#039;m pretty sure Raalf has a $500 a day crack habit). We&#039;re hoping to have this monstrosity of artistic brilliance done by the end of this week. (Only 6 months in production, wooohoo!). Our forums are up and running and very active.<br /><br />So, after my excessively long diatribe, where does this leave you all? Well, I&#039;d like to see us all together in one happy spot. You are after all about to become part of Quellious and the community.<br /><br />As Raalf said earlier, feel free to come by and register. Post a hello or F&#039;Tattle. We have two boards, one for EverQuest 1&amp;2 and one for WoW (part of the by product of moving from ezboard was that we have been unable to merge those two forums into one database, sorry). Our rules are very very close to your own here. Our flame section is very very lightly moderated. Say whatever you want, just don&#039;t bring RL information into play and don&#039;t post porn or really graphic nastiness.<br /><br />I invite the admins of this site to toss me an e-mail. I&#039;d like to see if we can work together throughout this process.<br /><br />If you have any concerns or questions, please e-mail me.<br /><br /><br /><img src="http://www.quellious-collective.com/pics/ravenark.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br /><a href="mailto:ravenark@quellious-collective.com">ravenark@quellious-collective.com</a><br /><a href="http://www.quellious-collective.com" target="_blank">www.quellious-collective.com</a><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
